.*
.* WRKWTR: the printers and their writers. View 1 is the V7R1M0
.* capture's (golden/verified/oracle71/panels): the file a writer is
.* printing; view 2 its output queue and how many files it printed.
:PNLGRP.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE=ACTION.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=STSCL BASETYPE='CHAR 4'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=SEPCL BASETYPE='CHAR 5'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=CNTCL BASETYPE='ZONED 5 0'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=VIEWCL BASETYPE='CHAR 1'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPT CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=WRITER CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=DEVICE CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=STATUS CLASS=STSCL.
:VAR NAME=SEP CLASS=SEPCL.
:VAR NAME=FORMTYPE CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=FILE CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=USER CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=USRDTA CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=OUTQ CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=LIB CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=PRINTED CLASS=CNTCL.
:VAR NAME=WVIEW CLASS=VIEWCL VALUE='1'.
:COND NAME=VIEW1 EXPR='&WVIEW. EQ "1"'.
:COND NAME=VIEW2 EXPR='&WVIEW. EQ "2"'.
:LISTDEF NAME=WRITERS VARS='OPT WRITER DEVICE STATUS SEP FORMTYPE FILE USER USRDTA OUTQ LIB PRINTED'.
:KEYL NAME=WTRKEYS HELP='KEYS/WTRKEYS'.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F11 ACTION='RETURN 11' COND=VIEW1.F11=View 2
:KEYI KEY=F11 ACTION='RETURN 11' COND=VIEW2.F11=View 1
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F17 ACTION=TOP.F17=Top
:KEYI KEY=F18 ACTION=BOTTOM.F18=Bottom
:KEYI KEY=F24 ACTION=MOREKEYS.F24=More keys
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.F5=Refresh
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKWTR KEYL=WTRKEYS HELP=WRKWTR ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SPACE.Work with All Printers
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=WRITERS VIEWS=2.(No printers)
:LISTACT OPTION=1 ENTER='CMD ?STRPRTWTR DEV(&DEVICE.)' HELP='WRKWTR/OPTIONS'.1=Start
:LISTACT OPTION=2 ENTER='CMD ?CHGWTR WTR(&WRITER.)' HELP='WRKWTR/OPTIONS'.2=Change
:LISTACT OPTION=3 ENTER='CMD HLDWTR WTR(&WRITER.)' HELP='WRKWTR/OPTIONS'.3=Hold
:LISTACT OPTION=4 ENTER='CMD ?ENDWTR WTR(&WRITER.)' HELP='WRKWTR/OPTIONS'.4=End
:LISTACT OPTION=5 ENTER='CMD WRKWTR WTR(&WRITER.)' HELP='WRKWTR/OPTIONS'.5=Work with
:LISTACT OPTION=6 ENTER='CMD RLSWTR WTR(&WRITER.)' HELP='WRKWTR/OPTIONS'.6=Release
:LISTACT OPTION=7 ENTER='CMD DSPMSG' HELP='WRKWTR/OPTIONS'.7=Display messages
:LISTACT OPTION=8 ENTER='CMD WRKOUTQ OUTQ(&LIB./&OUTQ.)' HELP='WRKWTR/OPTIONS'.8=Work with output queue
:LISTCOL VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT HELP='WRKWTR/OPT'.Opt
:LISTCOL VAR=DEVICE USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/DEVICE'.Device
:LISTCOL VAR=STATUS USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/STATUS'.Sts
:LISTCOL VAR=SEP USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/SEP'.Sep
:LISTCOL VAR=FORMTYPE USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/FORMTYPE'.Form Type
:LISTCOL VAR=FILE USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/FILE'.File
:LISTCOL VAR=USER USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/USER'.User
:LISTCOL VAR=USRDTA USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/USRDTA'.User Data
:LISTCOL VAR=WRITER USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/WRITER'.Writer
:LISTCOL VAR=OUTQ USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/OUTQ'.Output Queue
:LISTCOL VAR=LIB USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/LIB'.Library
:LISTCOL VAR=PRINTED USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/PRINTED'.Printed
:LISTVIEW COLS='OPT DEVICE STATUS SEP FORMTYPE FILE USER USRDTA'.
:LISTVIEW COLS='OPT DEVICE STATUS WRITER OUTQ LIB PRINTED'.
:ELIST.
:CMDLINE SIZE=SHORT.Parameters for options 1, 2, 3, 4, 6 or command
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=WRKWTR.Work with Printers - Help
:P.The printers with a writer started: what each is printing now, and
with F11 the output queue it takes files from and how many it has
printed.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/WTRKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F11=View 2
:PD.View 2.
:PT.F11=View 1
:PD.View 1.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:PT.F17=Top
:PD.Moves to the top of the list.
:PT.F18=Bottom
:PD.Moves to the bottom of the list.
:PT.F24=More keys
:PD.Shows the other function keys of the display.
:PT.F4=Prompt
:PD.Prompts the command on the command line, or the command of the
option typed.
:PT.F5=Refresh
:PD.Shows the display again with the current information.
:PT.F9=Retrieve
:PD.Puts the last command run back on the command line; press it again
for the one before.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKWTR/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/DEVICE'.Device
:P.The device the data goes to.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/STATUS'.Sts
:P.The sts of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SEP'.Sep
:P.The sep of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/FORMTYPE'.Form Type
:P.The type of form the output is printed on. The writer stops for the
form to be loaded when it changes.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/FILE'.File
:P.The file, by name and library.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/USER'.User
:P.The user of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/USRDTA'.User Data
:P.User data, up to 10 characters, kept with the object.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/WRITER'.Writer
:P.The writer&colon. the job that prints the spooled files of an output
queue.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/OUTQ'.Output Queue
:P.The output queue the spooled files go to.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/LIB'.Library
:P.The library of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/PRINTED'.Printed
:P.The printed of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKWTR/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.1=Start
:PD.Type 1 next to an entry and press Enter to start it. The Start
Printer Writer (STRPRTWTR) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.2=Change
:PD.Type 2 next to an entry and press Enter to change it. The Change
Writer (CHGWTR) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.3=Hold
:PD.Type 3 next to an entry and press Enter to hold it. The Hold Writer
(HLDWTR) command runs for the entry.
:PT.4=End
:PD.Type 4 next to an entry and press Enter to end it. The End Writer
(ENDWTR) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.5=Work with
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to work with it. The Work
with Writers (WRKWTR) command runs for the entry.
:PT.6=Release
:PD.Type 6 next to an entry and press Enter to release it. The Release
Writer (RLSWTR) command runs for the entry.
:PT.7=Display messages
:PD.Type 7 next to an entry and press Enter to display messages it. The
Display Messages (DSPMSG) command runs for the entry.
:PT.8=Work with output queue
:PD.Type 8 next to an entry and press Enter to work with output queue
it. The Work with Output Queue (WRKOUTQ) command runs for the entry.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
